WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.369
-It is the end of the week,
and that's usually when

00:00:03.369 --> 00:00:04.737
I catch up on
some personal stuff.

00:00:04.737 --> 00:00:06.606
You know, I check my inbox,
I return some e-mails,

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:08.607
and, of course,
I send out Thank You Notes.

00:00:08.607 --> 00:00:10.676
And I was just --
-[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.676 --> 00:00:12.512
I was running -- I was
running a bit behind today,

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:14.013
so I thought
if you guys wouldn't mind,

00:00:14.013 --> 00:00:15.915
I'd just like to write out
my weekly Thank You Notes

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:17.250
right now. Is that cool?

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.886
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:21.788
James -- James, can I get some

00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:23.656
Thank You Note writing music,
please?

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:24.957
-Wow.

00:00:24.957 --> 00:00:26.292
♪♪

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:27.727
-Wow.
-Don't break.

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:30.797
-He's bringin' it for 1,500.
-Yeah, he is. Yeah.

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:33.699
-Wow.

00:00:33.699 --> 00:00:35.335
♪♪

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:38.237
-Thank you, CDC mask guidelines,

00:00:38.237 --> 00:00:41.174
for basically just now being
the shrug emoji.

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:42.574
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.574 --> 00:00:44.911
"Yeah. I don't know."

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:46.312
-Yeah.

00:00:48.714 --> 00:00:50.116
♪♪

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:51.650
-Thank you, vaccine cards.

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:54.253
Sure, you might be
an irreplaceable document

00:00:54.253 --> 00:00:56.622
that I have to
carry around everywhere,

00:00:56.622 --> 00:00:58.691
but at least
you're made of flimsy paper

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:00.126
and don't fit in my wallet.

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:01.561
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:03.696
Why would you make these gi--

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:06.332
-"Might go a little bigger.
Just a little bigger."

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:08.935
-[ Laughs ]
Just a little bit bigger, yeah.

00:01:10.903 --> 00:01:12.371
♪♪

00:01:12.371 --> 00:01:15.474
Thank you, United Airlines,
for becoming the first

00:01:15.474 --> 00:01:19.412
major carrier to require
all employees to be vaccinated.

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:21.247
And thank you, Delta Airlines,

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:24.150
for continuing to hope this
name thing blows over soon.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.685
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:27.753
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:27.753 --> 00:01:30.757
-"Epsilon, please?"

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.394
♪♪

00:01:35.394 --> 00:01:37.329
-Thank you, "Dune,"

00:01:37.329 --> 00:01:39.899
or as I like to call you,
emo "Star Wars."

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:42.168
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:48.440
♪♪

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:50.976
Thank you,
laundry-detergent commercials,

00:01:50.976 --> 00:01:52.478
for really overestimating

00:01:52.478 --> 00:01:54.380
how often I passionately
caress my towels.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:56.716
[ Applause ]

00:01:58.984 --> 00:02:00.653
-"That's the dog's towel!"

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:01.987
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.987 --> 00:02:03.723
"I know."
-"We don't have a dog."

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:05.725
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:08.595
♪♪

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:10.296
Thank you, study that found

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:13.633
that headphone use
can lead to loneliness.

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:17.103
I think I speak for all
headphone users when I say...

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:18.604
"I'm sorry. What?"

00:02:18.604 --> 00:02:20.673
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:26.712
-Oh, wow.
Put your headphones away.

00:02:26.712 --> 00:02:28.548
Make sure you put
your earbuds away.

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:30.416
Oh, you play --
You're charging them.

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:31.417
Oh, that's good.

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:33.018
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.018 --> 00:02:34.653
Those the new ones?
-What's that?

00:02:34.653 --> 00:02:35.855
-Are those new ones?

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:37.290
-Yeah, you want
to check them out?

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:38.758
-Yeah. Let me see them.
-Check these out.

00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:41.293
-Oh. Wow!

00:02:41.293 --> 00:02:44.563
-Yeah, they're longer
than the other -- the other --

00:02:44.563 --> 00:02:47.399
Yeah, they're much longer. Yep.

00:02:47.399 --> 00:02:49.368
-[ Grunts ]
-That one has a twist on it.

00:02:49.368 --> 00:02:50.837
-Yeah.
-Yep. Stop.

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:52.772
No, you put it in backwards.
-Oh.

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:55.308
-Yeah. All right.
-Yep, perfect.

00:02:55.308 --> 00:02:57.610
♪♪

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.479
Oh, there --
Do you know what I'm saying?

00:02:59.479 --> 00:03:01.147
What do you think?
-What?!

00:03:01.147 --> 00:03:04.550
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:05.952
Here. Here you go.

00:03:05.952 --> 00:03:08.554
[ Applause ]

00:03:08.554 --> 00:03:10.723
-Oh, wait.
You're sewing them shut.

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:12.425
Wait!

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:16.262
It's pretty cool.

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:18.564
Wanna play with them, Tariq?
Check these out.

00:03:18.564 --> 00:03:23.602
♪♪

00:03:23.602 --> 00:03:25.204
Well?
-Wow.

00:03:25.204 --> 00:03:27.140
-Yeah, he digs it.
You like it?

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:29.342
-Yeah. I usually --
I just do the one ear.

00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:31.077
-Oh, you're one of those guys.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:33.312
-You're one of those guys.
-I'm sorry?!

00:03:33.312 --> 00:03:36.115
-You're o--
Is the other ear clogged?

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:38.017
-No. I'm sorry.
The other ear is --

00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:39.285
This ear's fine.

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:42.521
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.521 --> 00:03:43.890
-Give those back.
-One ear is dead?

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.491
-Give those back, dude.
I got to charge them up, man.

00:03:45.491 --> 00:03:47.460
Thanks. All right.
There we go.

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:51.397
[ Applause ]

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:55.768
♪♪

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:58.437
Thank you,
traveling summer carnivals.

00:03:58.437 --> 00:04:01.106
Nothing relaxes me
on a rusty wobbly ride

00:04:01.106 --> 00:04:03.276
like the knowledge
that you guys can skip town

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:04.610
as quickly as possible.

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:06.746
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:08.247
Yeah.

00:04:08.247 --> 00:04:10.617
[Inhales sharply]
"I think it's safe."

00:04:11.917 --> 00:04:14.019
-"Quick! Let's get outta here!"

00:04:14.019 --> 00:04:16.589
"Why's your car running?"
"No reason."

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:20.860
♪♪

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:22.628
-Thank you, sharks,

00:04:22.628 --> 00:04:25.197
for not going by your original
name, "murder dolphins."

00:04:25.197 --> 00:04:27.734
Thank you very much!
Those are our Thank You Notes.

